        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Murray cod: $\\frac{15}{40}=\\frac{3}{8}$; Redfin: $\\frac{10}{40}=\\frac{1}{4}$; Catfish: $\\frac{12}{40}=\\frac{3}{10}$; Murray perch: $\\frac{3}{40}$.",
          "worked": "Sample size: $15+10+12+3=40$.\n\nRelative frequency is the category frequency divided by the sample size.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Murray cod relative frequency}&=\\frac{15}{40}=\\frac{3}{8}\\\\\\text{Redfin relative frequency}&=\\frac{10}{40}=\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\\text{Catfish relative frequency}&=\\frac{12}{40}=\\frac{3}{10}\\\\\\text{Murray perch relative frequency}&=\\frac{3}{40}\\end{align*}$$",
